#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Title      : Arguments of hwla2vcd.py for the HWLA of PicoSoC, OpenBlaze8
# Project    : PicoSoC
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File       : hwla_openblaze8.args
# Author     : mrosiere
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: --args-file of tools/hwla2vcd.py of asylum-debug-hwla (>= 3.1.0 :
#              --signal, # comments), one argument per line :
#                python3 hwla2vcd.py capture.bin --args-file tools/hwla/hwla_openblaze8.args -o capture.vcd
#              HWLA of PicoSoC_top (DEBUG_ENABLE) with CPU_MODEL OpenBlaze8, the
#              default HWLA_* generics and the SoC clock of the NG-MEDIUM
#              targets (FSYS_INT 12.5 MHz) ; another configuration : change
#              -d, -p, -t, --period. One named signal per field of the
#              probes (README, Debug: HWLA), the bus of the user CPU
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copyright (c) 2026
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Revisions  :
# Date        Version  Author   Description
# 2026-11-27  1.0      mrosiere Created
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Probes : 4 strobes, address, write and read data of the data bus, fetch
# strobe, address and instruction of the instruction bus
-n
57
# HWLA_DEPTH : samples of a capture
-d
64
# HWLA_PRE_TRIGGER : samples before the trigger sample
-p
32
# HWLA_TIMESTAMP_WIDTH : timestamp of a sample (SoC clock cycles)
-t
16
# Bytes of the capture : 8-bit beats (UART or jtag_axis)
-w
8
# Period of the SoC clock (ns) : FSYS_INT 12.5 MHz
--period
80

# Data bus
--signal=dcs=0
--signal=dre=1
--signal=dwe=2
--signal=dready=3
--signal=daddr=11:4
--signal=dwdata=19:12
--signal=drdata=27:20
# Instruction bus : fetch strobe (the ROM gives the instruction the next
# cycle), address and instruction (output of the ROM)
--signal=ics=28
--signal=iaddr=38:29
--signal=idata=56:39
